# Normalize every text file to LF in both the index and the working tree.
#
# The tree was mixed: 76 files checked out CRLF and 38 as LF, under
# `core.autocrlf=true` with no attribute file to say which was intended. That mix
# is what made exact-match editing unreliable — a patch written against one file's
# convention silently failed against another's — and the workaround it produced
# (newline-agnostic scripts) is what corrupted source files more than once.
#
# The index was already LF for every tracked file, so checking these out as LF
# changes no content: the conversion shows up as an empty diff.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Anything binary is declared rather than detected, so a future asset cannot be
# silently mangled by the rule above.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
